            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="THU01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Edward</forename>
                        <surname>Thurlow</surname>
                        <addName>first Baron Thurlow</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1731-12-09">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1806-09-12"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <occupation>judge</occupation>
                    <occupation>lord chancellor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin notes his death on 9 December 1806.</p>
                        <p>There are two later entries:
      15.12.1813: 'Write to Thurlow.' <lb/>
      27.4.1815: 'W Curran calls n ( Thurlow ).' <lb/>
       These may refer to the second Baron <persName key="THU02">Thurlow</persName>, but we
    have no confirming evidence for this. On the other hand, there are no alternative candidates. 
   On 6 June 1829 Godwin records the death of the second Baron Thurlow, Edward 
   Hovell Thurlow (1781-1829), poet.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
